<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc Q2 shr down.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Q2 shr down.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in millions of dollars, except EPS)</p>
<p>		   RHONE-POULENC RORER INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>(Unaudited - amounts in millions except per share data)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					     June 30,	June 30,</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> NET SALES		    $1,238.0 $1,346.1 $2,323.8 $2,618.5</p>
<p> Cost of products sold	 367.0    443.8    691.4    878.0</p>
<p>Selling, delivery and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses    500.4    532.5    946.2  1,046.7</p>
<p>Research and development expenses</p>
<p>				     220.2    214.4    405.2    414.3</p>
<p> OPERATING INCOME		150.4    155.4    281.0    279.5</p>
<p> Interest expense - net	 37.5     43.5     76.2     84.5</p>
<p> Other (income)- net(A)(B)  (15.4)   (36.6)   (20.8)   (77.4)</p>
<p> INCOME BEFORE INCOME TAXES  128.3    148.5    225.6    272.4</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes   39.6     46.3     70.1     85.2</p>
<p>Dividends on preferred stock</p>
<p>and remuneration on</p>
<p>  capital equity notes	  11.8     10.3     21.9     21.3</p>
<p>NET INCOME AVAILABLE TO</p>
<p> COMMON SHAREHOLDERS	    76.9     91.9    133.6    165.9</p>
<p> Earnings Per Common Share     .56	.68	.98     1.23</p>
<p>Average Common Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding		    137.1    135.7    137.0    135.3</p>
<p>(A)  Losses from equity affiliates, principally the Company's interest in the Centeon joint venture, totaled $14.2 million and $19.8 million, respectively, for the three-and six-month periods ending June 30, 1997. Negative contributions from Centeon in 1997 included the impact of recall-related and manufacturing start-up costs associated with its U.S. production facility totaling $13.3 million and $31.5 million for the quarter and six months, respectively. Income from equity affiliates totaled $40.6 million and $77.7 million, respectively, for the comparable 1996 periods.</p>
<p>(B)  Other (income)-net for the three and six-months ended June 30, 1997, included a pretax gain of $16.0 million ($.08 per share) on the termination of a partnership arrangement with Watson Pharmaceuticals, Inc. in connection with the June 1997 licensing to Watson of the distribution rights to diltiazem products.</p>
